slml 0.2
use"layout.slml"

doc{$title"The SLML Handbook"
  t.lead"SLML, the *Strict Layout Markup Language*, is a short, strict language for web pages and documents. One small grammar replaces HTML and CSS, and layout is built in. You write `.slml` files and the `slml` native browser reads and draws them directly."
  demo{$code"""
      slml 0.2
      page{
        #"Hello!"
        r{g12 a:c
          btn{>#why "About me"}
          "Made with *SLML*"
        }
      }
      """
    #"Hello!"
    r{g12 a:c
      btn{>#why "About me"}
      "Made with *SLML*"
    }
  }
  section{$id"why" $title"Why SLML?"
    -{g8
      "*Short.* `c{p20 bg#fff \"Hi\"}` is a padded white box with a paragraph. Frequent things cost one or two characters."
      "*Strict.* A mistake is an error with a line number and a hint, never a silently broken page."
      "*Layout, not semantics.* Rows, columns, grids, gaps and alignment are the language. There is no `main`, `aside` or `section` with rules about where each may go."
      "*One syntax.* Structure, appearance and reusable components share one grammar instead of three languages."
      "*Predictable.* Fonts are bundled and every default is written down, so a page looks the same everywhere."
      "*Accessible.* Images must describe themselves and form fields must have labels."
    }
  }
  section{$id"how" $title"How it works"
    "The native browser is the normal way to use SLML:"
    +{g8
      "*Open a page or site.* Run `slml page.slml` or `slml my-site/`. SLML opens its own window, parses the original source and draws it with its Rust renderer."
      "*Edit and save.* The window reloads when the page, an import or an image changes. Local links stay in SLML."
      "*Use adapters only when you choose them.* `slml build` explicitly exports HTML. The optional `slml serve --web` runtime and the Firefox extension host SLML in existing web browsers."
    }
  }
  section{$id"start" $title"Where to start"
    grid{cw220 g14
      c.tile{>/install.slml
        ####"1. Install"
        t.muted"Get the slml program for Linux, macOS or Windows."
      }
      c.tile{>/first-page.slml
        ####"2. First page"
        t.muted"Write and open your first page in five minutes."
      }
      c.tile{>/syntax.slml
        ####"3. Learn the syntax"
        t.muted"Everything SLML can say, on one page."
      }
    }
  }
  note{$title"This handbook is written in SLML"
    "Every page you are reading is an `.slml` file in the `handbook/` folder of the repository. Open them to see real-world SLML."
  }
  pager{$prev"/reference.slml" $prev-label"Reference" $next"/install.slml" $next-label"Install SLML"}
}
